WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.673
A pharmaceutical launch can look busy and still be exposed.

00:00:03.673 --> 00:00:12.028
Weak assumptions, missing evidence, disconnected workstreams, and late decisions often become visible only after the cost of change has climbed.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:28.450
RxLaunchOS starts with the actual launch context: the product, indication, timeline, commercial objectives, constraints, available evidence, and the leaders accountable for each consequential decision.

00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:36.282
The readiness layer distinguishes what is known, assumed, missing, stale, contradictory, or blocked.

00:00:36.282 --> 00:00:44.373
When the evidence is insufficient, it refuses false precision and shows the work needed before the plan can be trusted.

00:00:45.383 --> 00:01:00.505
Teams can structure the operating model, field force, CRM timing, partner requirements, requests for proposal, territory design, milestones, and dependencies—while preserving the evidence and assumptions behind each choice.

00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:04.381
Scenario Lab compares explicit options.

00:01:04.381 --> 00:01:07.246
Internal versus outsourced field teams.

00:01:07.246 --> 00:01:09.229
Different hiring sequences.

00:01:09.229 --> 00:01:11.065
CRM and territory timing.

00:01:11.065 --> 00:01:19.071
Each scenario shows assumptions, tradeoffs, dependencies, leading indicators, and the consequence of waiting.

00:01:19.071 --> 00:01:21.422
It is comparison—not prediction.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:30.141
Human-approved decisions carry into accountable work, milestones, risks, reports, and launch signals.

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:40.497
RxLaunchOS can explain and challenge the plan, but it cannot silently approve a gate or make the commercial decision for leadership.

00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:47.455
The result is one operating rhythm: define, diagnose, design, decide, operate, and learn.

00:01:47.455 --> 00:01:58.264
